# 📏 Spread of Three
# Try to give every 2×2 square a spread of exactly 3. Each 2×2 square with a spread of exactly 3
# scores 1 primary point. Each square deducts 1 secondary point for each step its spread is away
# from 3. A square's spread is its biggest number minus its smallest: 7, 4, 5 and 6 spread 7 − 4 =
